@startuml Tuba_Glider_State_Machine
title Tuba Glider Application State Machine

[*] --> POWERUP_WAIT

POWERUP_WAIT --> MENU: EVT_ENTER\n(user presses ENTER)
POWERUP_WAIT --> DEPLOYED: EVT_TIMEOUT\n(startup countdown expires)

MENU --> PARAMS_MENU: "1" / parameters
MENU --> HWTEST_MENU: "2" / hardware test
MENU --> SIMULATE: "3" / simulate deployment
MENU --> DEPLOYED: "4" / deploy\n[external pressure sensor present]
MENU --> OTA_MENU: "5" / firmware update

PARAMS_MENU --> PARAM_INPUT: "1-m" / select parameter
PARAMS_MENU --> PARAMS_MENU: "s" / save\n"r" / reset defaults
PARAMS_MENU --> MENU: "x" / back

PARAM_INPUT --> PARAMS_MENU: value entered / [accepted or rejected]

HWTEST_MENU --> PR_MENU: "1" / pitch & roll
HWTEST_MENU --> PUMP_INPUT: "2" / pump test
HWTEST_MENU --> HWTEST_MENU: "3" positions\n"4" internal pressure\n"5" external pressure\n"6" GPS\n"8" leak sensor\n"a" I2C scan report
HWTEST_MENU --> COMPASS_MENU: "7" / compass
HWTEST_MENU --> SENSORS_MENU: "9" / sensors
HWTEST_MENU --> MENU: "x" / back

SENSORS_MENU --> TEMP_MENU: "1" / temperature
SENSORS_MENU --> HWTEST_MENU: "x" / back

TEMP_MENU --> TEMP_MENU: "1" self-test\n"2" stream
TEMP_MENU --> SENSORS_MENU: "x" / back

PR_MENU --> PR_INPUT: "1" roll motor\n"2" pitch motor
PR_MENU --> PR_MENU: "3" / limit switch test
PR_MENU --> HWTEST_MENU: "x" / back

PR_INPUT --> PR_INPUT: integer / run motor [-10..10 s]
PR_INPUT --> PR_MENU: "q" / quit

PUMP_INPUT --> PUMP_INPUT: integer / run pump [-10..10 s]
PUMP_INPUT --> HWTEST_MENU: "q" / quit

COMPASS_MENU --> COMPASS_MENU: "1" calibrate\n"2" stream heading
COMPASS_MENU --> HWTEST_MENU: "x" / back

OTA_MENU --> MENU: "x" / cancel
OTA_MENU --> MENU: download or verify failed
OTA_MENU --> [*]: verified / reboot into new firmware

DEPLOYED --> MENU: mission complete\n[worker finished, no abort]
DEPLOYED --> RECOVERY: safety guard tripped\n[worker finished, deploy_aborted()]

SIMULATE --> MENU: simulation complete\n[worker finished, no abort]
SIMULATE --> RECOVERY: safety guard tripped\n[worker finished, deploy_aborted()]

RECOVERY --> DEPLOYED: "resume"
RECOVERY --> MENU: "menu"
RECOVERY --> RECOVERY: (other input)

note right of POWERUP_WAIT
    Startup countdown
    (STARTUP_TIMEOUT_SEC = 600 s)
    waiting for user intervention.
    Prevents accidental deployment.

    on_entry: prints countdown
    on_exit: newline cleanup
end note

note right of MENU
    Main control center. Header shows
    build number, UTC time (+source)
    and console input mode.
end note

note right of PARAMS_MENU
    Edit mission parameters:
    - dive depth / timing
    - pitch/roll/pump positions
    - desired heading
    - leak threshold
    - console input mode (UART/WiFi)
    - safety envelope (h-m):
      T_MISSION, depth limit,
      sensor retries, full-stroke
      times, recovery interval

    Stored in NVS; "s" saves,
    edits alone are RAM-only.
end note

note right of SENSORS_MENU
    Sensor diagnostics:
    - TSYS01 water temperature
      self-test (probe, PROM,
      sample plausibility)
    - live temperature stream
end note

note right of HWTEST_MENU
    "a" I2C scan report:
    expected-sensor I2C scan
    (connected vs missing)
end note

note right of DEPLOYED
    Mission worker thread:
    1. surface reference pressure
    2. wait deploy_wait_s
    3. GPS fix (syncs UTC clock)
    4. dive to depth / timeout
    5. apogee (swing to climb trim)
    6. climb to surface
    7. GPS fix, 10 s ENTER window
    8. repeat until ENTER

    Every second: a [SENS] line
    (UTC, hull pressure, depth,
    water temp, attitude) and a
    machine-readable $D row.

    Each phase is bounded by the
    safety envelope; a breach
    aborts to RECOVERY instead of
    completing the cycle.
end note

note right of SIMULATE
    Same worker as DEPLOYED but
    depth is synthetic (0.5 m/s
    sink/rise) — bench testing
    without a pressure sensor.
end note

note right of RECOVERY
    Entered when a safety guard
    trips: T_MISSION (or half of
    it with no climb yet), depth
    limit, depth-sensor failure,
    or a leak.

    The worker has already parked
    the glider in the RECOVERY
    POSITION -- pump fully OUT,
    pitch fully FORWARD, roll
    neutral -- and held station,
    reporting every T_RSLEEP min
    until the operator pressed
    ENTER.

    on_entry prints the abort
    cause. "resume" re-deploys,
    "menu" returns to the top.
end note

@enduml
